{
  "audio": "024.verification-works-best.mp3",
  "paragraph": 24,
  "text": "Verification works best when it is enforced by code, not by prompt begging. Every builder has tried writing strict warnings in a system prompt, like never touch the environment file and always run the typechecker, only to watch the model forget twenty turns later. Harnesses like Claude Code replace prompt begging with deterministic lifecycle hooks. A pre-tool-use hook inspects every tool call before it runs and blocks secret files outright. A post-tool-use hook fires automatically after an edit, running TypeScript checks and targeted tests without relying on model willpower.",
  "transcript": "Verification works best when it is enforced by code, not by prompt begging. Every builder has tried writing strict warnings in a system prompt, like never touch the environment file and always run the type checker, only to watch the model forget 20 turns later. Harnesses like Claude Code replace prompt begging with deterministic lifecycle hooks. A pre-tool use hook inspects every tool call before it runs and blocks secret files outright. A post-tool use hook fires automatically after an edit, it, running TypeScript checks and targeted tests without relying on model willpower.",
